2. llms-full budget: test that byte-length is enforced — build text with non-ASCII to exceed budget in bytes but not chars? Budget is 150KB; constructing over-budget content is awkward. Alternative test: call buildLlmsFull with a huge llmsTxt of repeated '—' where char count < budget but byte count > budget, expect StateError. E.g. llmsTxt with 80,000 '—' chars → 160,000 bytes > 153,600. That works. Also a test that guard passes at high-but-within byte budget... simpler: assert throws for non-ASCII overflow.
