Fixed — arg parsing is now strict via a pure, unit-tested `parseArgs(List<String>)`:

- returns the `--out` value (`null` = in-tree build), exactly the previous pairing logic;
- throws `FormatException` on any unrecognized arg (`--outdir`, trailing junk, bare positionals), on `--out` without a value, and on the removed `--check` (message carries the migration hint);
- `main` catches it, prints `usage: dart scripts/build_site.dart [--out <dir>]`, and exits 2 — so `dart scripts/build_site.dart --outdir /tmp/x` now fails fast instead of silently building into `site/`.

Verified end-to-end: `--outdir /tmp/x`, bare `--out`, and `junk` all exit 2 with usage; `--out <dir>` builds correctly. Five new `parseArgs` tests cover the happy path and every red path (all fail pre-fix).

